{"raw": {"https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/lecturer-of-music-industry-arts-administration-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {"title": "Lecturer of Music Industry: Arts Administration", "description": "Lecturer of Music Industry: Arts Administration - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Lecturer of Music Industry: Arts Administration - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer of Music Industry: Arts Administration 20002365 College of Visual and Performing Arts Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Oct 16 2026 Academic Affairs 100028 - School of Music Working Title: Lecturer of Music Industry: Arts Administration State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Visual and Performing Arts Department: 100028 - School of Music Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 11/16/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia\u2019s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master\u2019s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The School of Music at James Madison University seeks an exceptional and experienced arts administrator and teacher for a full-time, RTA Lecturer of Music Industry: Arts Administration, to begin in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a proven track record in arts management including fundraising, marketing and the production of both traditional and non-traditional artistic experiences. Our new colleague will bring a vision for audience development, community engagement, and innovative strategies aligned with the changing cultural landscape. The successful candidate will join a dynamic, collaborative, and collegial team of artist faculty who are working together to build and execute a curriculum that is just and responsive to the needs of the next generation of arts administrators and music industry professionals. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include creating and implement an engaging Arts Administration curriculum within the existing undergraduate Music Industry curriculum. Our new colleague will also demonstrate interest and engagement with campus programming, with an eye toward creative marketing and audience development. Other duties may be assigned based on the skills and experience of the candidate and departmental needs. In addition to teaching, the candidate will be expected to develop and maintain a visible profile locally, regionally, nationally, and internationally. Qualifications: Required qualifications include: \u2022 Master\u2019s Degree in Arts Administration \u2022 Bachelor or master\u2019s degree in music \u2022 5 years minimum successful professional experience in the field \u2022 Demonstrated success writing grants and fundraising \u2022 Tangible outcomes with audience building, and immersive, compelling production \u2022 A record of effective collaboration Preferred qualifications include: \u2022 Doctorate in Arts Administration \u2022 Familiarity in the use of digital media and/or interactive media \u2022 Active membership and/or leadership in professional organizations \u2022 A history of building partnerships between academic programs and local or regional arts organizations Additional Posting Information: The James Madison University School of Music is an active program with about 400 undergraduate majors, 75 graduate students (DMA and MM), and 200 music minors. The School of Music consists of 45 full-time faculty and 25 part-time faculty that produces more than 200 performances and presentations annually, promoting a vibrant culture of research, scholarship, and creative activity. Housed within the College of Visual and Performing Arts, the School of Music offers the Bachelor of Music in music performance, music education, composition, music theatre, and music industry; the Bachelor of Arts in Music with concentrations in Music Studies and Music Industry; Master\u2019s degrees in composition, conducting, music education, and music performance; and Doctoral degrees in Performance, Pedagogy and Literature and Conducting, Pedagogy and Literature. The College of Visual and Performing Arts strives to create an educational environment that inspires responsible citizenship. A complete application will include: a cover letter, a curriculum vitae; and names and contact information for three references. Additional materials may be requested later in the search process. JMU\u2019s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 76c742ec Last Name (required) bcacbca1 Email (required) 343deda7 Job Alert 6a1c2376 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) 29826bbc Last Name (required) d6f7d685 Email (required) ee7895f8 Who would you like to send this job to? 1b3c283b Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Administrative and Work Control Program Support 20002375 Administrative / Office Staff , Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) Facilities Management at JMU has an open position for an Administrative and Work Control Program Support. This position will serve as a coordinator & central point of contact in the Work Control department for techs, staff and customers on campus from origination to completion. This position will have the working hours of Monday- Friday 11am-7pm. Program Support Assistant (Part-Time), School of Professional & Continuing Education 20002374 Administrative / Office Staff Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried JMU\u2019s School of Professional & Continuing Education (SPCE) fosters learning across lifespans through transformative education and enrichment. SPCE offers a range of programs, including youth camps, adult degree completion, professional and workforce development, and lifelong learning, as well as partners with academic units across JMU to support a number of online or off-campus degree and certificate programs. This part-time role supports both the Lifelong Learning Institute (LLI) and Youth Programs within SPCE. The ideal candidate will assist with a variety of programmatic, logistical, and administrative tasks to ensure the success of events, courses, and activities across both programs. Integrated Pest Management Lead Technician 20002370 Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) James Madison University\u2019s Facilities Management is accepting applications for a Integrated Pest Management Technician. Shift is Monday \u2013 Friday, 6:30 a.m. \u2013 3:00 p.m., with overtime as required to cover special events and inclement weather. There is a slightly alternate schedule during the summer months. This position is eligible for a $2,000 sign-on bonus. $1,000 will be paid out after completing six months in the position and the remaining $1,000 will be paid out after completing 12 months in the position. Apply Now First Name (required) e457ae41 Last Name (required) d02eceaf Email (required) 3916b95e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 6b7c7b0a Last Name (required) 90663841 Email (required) 1a552737 Job Alert 1ae6f5f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-psychology-psychological-research-methodology-psychology-as-a-natural-science-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {"title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychology - Psychological Research Methodology & Psychology as a Natural Science", "description": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychology - Psychological Research Methodology & Psychology as a Natural Science - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychology - Psychological Research Methodology & Psychology as a Natural Science - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychology - Psychological Research Methodology & Psychology as a Natural Science 20002361 College of Health and Behavioral Studies Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Oct 15 2026 Academic Affairs 100053 - Psychology Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychology - Psychological Research Methodology & Psychology as a Natural Science State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Health and Behavioral Studies Department: 100053 - Psychology Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 11/16/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia\u2019s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master\u2019s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Department of Psychology in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University (JMU) invites applicants for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor and with a focus on teaching Psychological Research Methodology and one or more courses in our \u201cPsychology as a Natural Science\u201d core area, to begin August 2027. Our \u201cPsychology as a Natural Science\u201d curriculum content area includes Sensation and Perception Biopsychology, Cognitive Psychology, Psychology of Learning, and Comparative Animal Behavior. Please see https://catalog.jmu.edu/programs/psychology-ba/#requirementstext for the current curriculum. The new hire will join an enthusiastic pre-tenure cohort, as the department has been expanding and recently welcomed several new colleagues. CHBS is committed to shaping a forward-thinking and dynamic environment by refining policies, practices, and processes that strengthen our community, drive real-world advancement, and maintain spaces conducive to individual and collective growth. Through education, scholarship, and service, individuals are inspired to make responsible and meaningful contributions to the college, campus, local community, and broader world. Join us in fostering collaboration and innovation as we grow a dynamic college that embodies an atmosphere of belonging, champions excellence, and shares a sense of purpose. James Madison University is an equal opportunity employer committed to fostering a thriving environment where a wide range of perspectives are embraced, and fairness is upheld. More information about CHBS can be found here: https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/index.shtml. Duties and Responsibilities: Tenure-track faculty are expected to develop an active program of scholarship that involves undergraduate students in research. Supervision of independent research projects and honors thesis projects are typical components of an individual's teaching assignment. Occasional course instruction and supervision of graduate students enrolled in JMU's M.A. in Psychological Sciences Program may be possible (see https://psyc.jmu.edu/psycsciences/index.html for further information). Additionally, the successful candidate will be expected to serve as an academic advisor to Psychology majors and to contribute to the service activities of the department, college, and university, while often taking part in professional service as well. Psychology is among the most popular programs of study on campus, serving approximately 1200 undergraduate majors. JMU emphasizes instructional innovation in the classroom, evidence-based approaches to instructional improvements, and engaged learning experiences for undergraduates. With 29 full-time faculty members, the Department of Psychology is a strong contributor to these efforts. Additional information about psychology at JMU is available at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/psyc/index.shtml. JMU is a student-centered community that values excellence, integrity, and mutual respect. JMU highly values quality teaching, and the university has substantial infrastructure to support teaching, instructional technology, and faculty development, such as our Center for Faculty Innovation (jmu.edu/cfi). For more information about JMU see www.jmu.edu. Qualifications: Required qualifications for this position include: 1. PhD in Psychology, or ABD with a degree conferral date in or before August 2027. 2. A documented history of active engagement in scholarship. 3. Evidence of the ability to provide innovative instruction in Psychological Research Methodology, as well as one or more courses in our \u201cPsychology as a Natural Science\u201d core curriculum area (see list of courses above). 4. A demonstrated ability to to contribute to the service endeavors of our department. Preferred qualifications for this position include: 1. Evidence of incorporating best practices from the scholarship of teaching and learning, including the use of high-impact, evidence-based learning strategies in course assignments or design. 2. Evidence of peer-reviewed publications. 3. A demonstrated ability to provide high-quality mentoring to undergraduate students from a variety of backgrounds and perspectives. 4. A demonstrated ability to incorporate undergraduate students as active collaborators in scholarship. 5. A demonstrated ability to contribute to the service endeavors of our college, university, professional organizations, and/or community. Additional Posting Information: The mission of the Department of Psychology is \"to educate students in, and contribute to, the science of psychology.\" The successful candidate will contribute to teaching Psychological Research Methodology courses and other courses in their areas of expertise that meet our core curriculum area of \u201cPsychology as a Natural Science.\u201d To apply, go to jobs.jmu.edu. In addition to completing the faculty profile, the following materials should be submitted online: (1) Letter of Interest (2) Curriculum Vitae (3) Teaching Statement (including evidence of teaching quality) (4) Research Statement (including description of current/future research plans), submitted under \"Other Document #1\" (5) Names and contact information for three references. References will receive an email requesting that they provide a letter of recommendation after the first round of interviews. For questions, please contact Dr. Benjamin Blankenship (blankebt@jmu.edu, 540-568-4915). JMU\u2019s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d64d8d46 Last Name (required) 75736398 Email (required) cfd0aed7 Job Alert 65eb3f6a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) 32c3c4cb Last Name (required) a11c4848 Email (required) 12032e06 Who would you like to send this job to? ce8af5d0 Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Administrative and Work Control Program Support 20002375 Administrative / Office Staff , Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) Facilities Management at JMU has an open position for an Administrative and Work Control Program Support. This position will serve as a coordinator & central point of contact in the Work Control department for techs, staff and customers on campus from origination to completion. This position will have the working hours of Monday- Friday 11am-7pm. Program Support Assistant (Part-Time), School of Professional & Continuing Education 20002374 Administrative / Office Staff Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried JMU\u2019s School of Professional & Continuing Education (SPCE) fosters learning across lifespans through transformative education and enrichment. SPCE offers a range of programs, including youth camps, adult degree completion, professional and workforce development, and lifelong learning, as well as partners with academic units across JMU to support a number of online or off-campus degree and certificate programs. This part-time role supports both the Lifelong Learning Institute (LLI) and Youth Programs within SPCE. The ideal candidate will assist with a variety of programmatic, logistical, and administrative tasks to ensure the success of events, courses, and activities across both programs. Integrated Pest Management Lead Technician 20002370 Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) James Madison University\u2019s Facilities Management is accepting applications for a Integrated Pest Management Technician. Shift is Monday \u2013 Friday, 6:30 a.m. \u2013 3:00 p.m., with overtime as required to cover special events and inclement weather. There is a slightly alternate schedule during the summer months. This position is eligible for a $2,000 sign-on bonus. $1,000 will be paid out after completing six months in the position and the remaining $1,000 will be paid out after completing 12 months in the position. Apply Now First Name (required) 1598c5b1 Last Name (required) a6667412 Email (required) a587d7e3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 34f8a091 Last Name (required) 504a9b3b Email (required) 17e5d4ba Job Alert 30c3567b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/intelligence-analysis-assistant-associate-professor-or-assistant-associate-professor-of-practice-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {"title": "Intelligence Analysis - Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice", "description": "Intelligence Analysis - Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Intelligence Analysis - Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Intelligence Analysis - Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice 20002354 College of Integrated Science and Engineering Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Oct 13 2026 Academic Affairs 100060 - Integrated Science and Technology Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Intelligence Analysis - Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Integrated Science and Engineering Department: 100060 - Integrated Science and Technology Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 11/13/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia\u2019s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master\u2019s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: We invite applications for a faculty position in our Bachelor\u2019s Degree Program in Intelligence Analysis beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will be appointed either at the rank of tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor, or at the rank of RTA Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice, depending on qualifications and experience. In its 20th year, the Intelligence Analysis Program continues to be an in-demand, multidisciplinary undergraduate degree preparing students to become analysts, with a specialization in intelligence analysis. Our vision is a versatile education that simultaneously teaches students to synthesize both critical and creative thinking with data analytics for collection, interpretation, and visualization in the production and communication of analysis, frequently within a security context. Our program serves around 250 students, with important national and international partnerships to provide opportunities for students to apply their education directly to real-world security challenges. Our community is composed of teacher-scholars, and so a hallmark of our program is the meaningful involvement of undergraduate students in applied and scholarly work. The Intelligence Analysis Program resides within the broader School of Integrated Sciences (SIS), and the College of Integrated Science and Engineering. SIS supports innovative and dynamic academic careers for over 50 faculty rooted in three undergraduate programs: Geography, Integrated Science and Technology, and Intelligence Analysis, along with potential for renewed graduate programs. SIS is a vibrant, welcoming, and supportive culture that embraces innovation, collaboration, humility, and student engagement. We seek to balance and integrate both teaching and research, as well as specialized disciplines and distinctive degree programs, within an open and supportive culture. For more information about our School and its programs, please visit: https://www.jmu.edu/cise/sis/ Duties and Responsibilities: Our ideal future colleague would be an engaged teacher, in-depth scholar, and active contributor to the professional communities that support analysis. A typical teaching load is three in-person courses per semester. Our future colleague would begin by teaching our existing courses but also have the opportunity to assist in curricular development that further advances the teaching of analysis. We welcome applicants from any academic discipline (to include the humanities, social sciences, and natural sciences) and/or any professional analytical background in the public or private sectors that enables them to speak with credibility about the process of doing analysis and qualifies them to teach in (ideally) multiple areas of our curriculum, and to advance scholarship on analysis and in the disciplines that support it. We also value other internal and external professional service that improves the disciplines and communities that promote good analysis. Qualifications: A Ph.D. in a relevant academic field is required for a Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor appointment. A minimum of a master\u2019s degree in combination with substantial, demonstrated experience as an analyst is required for an RTA Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice appointment. Candidates should have sufficient education and/or experience to demonstrate the ability to teach specific courses in (ideally) two or more of the following areas of the IA Program: critical thinking and reasoning methodologies, data analytics, the social context and lived experience of analysts, and the development and delivery of analytic products. We are particularly interested in applicants who demonstrate commitment to: \u2022 Excellence in teaching undergraduates, as well as thoughtfulness about improving approaches to undergraduate education for analysis. \u2022 Professional mentoring of students seeking to become future analysts. \u2022 Significant potential as a scholar with a strategic and intentional research agenda. \u2022 Research focusing on the study and practice of analysis, to include, but not limited to, Intelligence Analysis. \u2022 Collaboration to support and expand the scope and reach of the IA Program, and corresponding opportunities for its students and faculty. Additional Posting Information: Required Documentation: 1. Cover Letter that explains specifically how the candidate\u2019s expertise and experience fit our particular Programmatic aspirations, values, and areas of teaching. 2. Curriculum Vitae. 3. Teaching Statement (of no more than 2 pages) that explains the candidate's approach to the theory and practice of teaching undergraduates. 4. Research Overview (of no more than 2 pages, uploaded under \"other document #1\") that explains the candidate's development as a scholar and how their work would help advance the future of analysis at JMU and beyond. JMU\u2019s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 8354dea2 Last Name (required) 6c1a1780 Email (required) 2f4c7988 Job Alert dd32b312 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching 