completing six months in the position and the remaining $1,000 will be paid out after completing 12 months in the position. Apply Now First Name (required) 70d421f8 Last Name (required) 28111de6 Email (required) 3a236b4d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) ae0ebea6 Last Name (required) 777f9fda Email (required) f4795017 Job Alert 2a1b287d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-physics-and-astronomy-tenure-track-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Physics and Astronomy (Tenure-Track)", "description": "Assistant Professor of Physics and Astronomy (Tenure-Track) - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of Physics and Astronomy (Tenure-Track) - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Physics and Astronomy (Tenure-Track) 20002327 College of Science and Mathematics Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Oct 1 2026 Academic Affairs 100032 - Physics Department Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Assistant Professor of Physics and Astronomy (Tenure-Track) State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Science and Mathematics Department: 100032 - Physics Department Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? N/A Beginning Review Date: 11/20/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia\u2019s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master\u2019s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Department of Physics and Astronomy at James Madison University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Physics with expertise in data-intensive, computational, and/or AI-enabled approaches to physics, astronomy, or closely related fields. This is a full-time appointment beginning August 10, 2027. The Department of Physics & Astronomy at James Madison University combines a strong commitment to undergraduate education with an active culture of scholarship and discovery. Through excellent teaching, close mentorship, and faculty-led research programs that engage undergraduate students, the department provides a rich educational experience for its majors. The department consists of 21 full-time faculty members, most of whom maintain active research agendas, and approximately 70 students enrolled in our multi-track baccalaureate-only programs. Please visit our website at http://www.jmu.edu/physics for more information about the department. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will contribute to the department's mission through outstanding teaching, active scholarship, and meaningful service. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate physics and/or astronomy courses and laboratories at both introductory and advanced levels. The candidate will establish and maintain an active, externally visible research program that engages undergraduate students and enhances the scholarly reputation of the department, college, and university. The successful candidate will also contribute to the continuing development of an innovative curriculum, including courses related to data science, computation, artificial intelligence, and other emerging areas relevant to the discipline and university priorities. Faculty participate in departmental, college, and university service activities that support the academic community, including committee work, student mentoring, and professional service. Qualifications: Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Physics, Astronomy, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Relevant Postdoctoral (or equivalent) experience is preferred. Candidates will be evaluated based on their potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching and their ability to establish a productive research program that actively involves undergraduate students. Preference will be given to candidates whose teaching and research interests include data-intensive, computational, and/or AI-enabled approaches to physics, astronomy, or closely related fields. Areas of interest may include, but are not limited to, computational astrophysics, data-driven astronomy, biophysics, materials physics, computational physics, or other emerging interdisciplinary areas. The department is particularly interested in candidates who have the potential to secure external funding and develop a sustained research program, as well as those interested in developing courses that integrate computing, data science, artificial intelligence, or other workforce-relevant skills. Interest in contributing to the university's General Education program, particularly the Science, Technology, and the Built Environment and/or Connections areas, and a commitment to mentoring undergraduate researchers are desirable. Additional Posting Information: To apply, complete the PageUp application and provide: \u2022 A cover letter addressing relevant qualifications \u2022 Current curriculum vitae (CV) \u2022 A Teaching Statement (uploaded under \u201cStatement of Teaching Philosophy\u201d) that describes your planned and/or ongoing approach to: * Effectively teach undergraduate students * Promote a welcoming and supportive climate for students in teaching and research \u2022 A statement of research (uploaded as \"Other Document #1) plans involving students at JMU with: * A 5-year plan that involves undergraduate students at JMU * Plans to promote the growth and excellence of student researchers \u2022The names and contact information for three professional references JMU\u2019s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 995c8981 Last Name (required) 42b73755 Email (required) 5e93dfc2 Job Alert 1741999b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) fb31e7b1 Last Name (required) f574e000 Email (required) 4fc62ea9 Who would you like to send this job to? d85054ad Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Administrative and Work Control Program Support 20002375 Administrative / Office Staff , Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) Facilities Management at JMU has an open position for an Administrative and Work Control Program Support. This position will serve as a coordinator & central point of contact in the Work Control department for techs, staff and customers on campus from origination to completion. This position will have the working hours of Monday- Friday 11am-7pm. Program Support Assistant (Part-Time), School of Professional & Continuing Education 20002374 Administrative / Office Staff Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried JMU\u2019s School of Professional & Continuing Education (SPCE) fosters learning across lifespans through transformative education and enrichment. SPCE offers a range of programs, including youth camps, adult degree completion, professional and workforce development, and lifelong learning, as well as partners with academic units across JMU to support a number of online or off-campus degree and certificate programs. This part-time role supports both the Lifelong Learning Institute (LLI) and Youth Programs within SPCE. The ideal candidate will assist with a variety of programmatic, logistical, and administrative tasks to ensure the success of events, courses, and activities across both programs. Integrated Pest Management Lead Technician 20002370 Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) James Madison University\u2019s Facilities Management is accepting applications for a Integrated Pest Management Technician. Shift is Monday \u2013 Friday, 6:30 a.m. \u2013 3:00 p.m., with overtime as required to cover special events and inclement weather. There is a slightly alternate schedule during the summer months. This position is eligible for a $2,000 sign-on bonus. $1,000 will be paid out after completing six months in the position and the remaining $1,000 will be paid out after completing 12 months in the position. Apply Now First Name (required) 48e34cde Last Name (required) 0df67554 Email (required) e33799bd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 1cf04dac Last Name (required) b4257575 Email (required) b104043b Job Alert 0e5777d8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/physician-assistant-studies-graduate-program-director-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {"title": "Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director", "description": "Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 College of Health and Behavioral Studies Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Sep 25 2026 Academic Affairs 100720 - Department of Health Professions Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Health and Behavioral Studies Department: 100720 - Department of Health Professions Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 10/26/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia\u2019s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master\u2019s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs. The successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will: 1. Teach graduate courses in the Physician Assistant Studies program. 2. Serve as the Program Director to oversee ARC-PA accreditation processes and ensure ongoing compliance with standards. 3. Provide strategic leadership for the program through oversight of program organization, administration, fiscal management, and continuous programmatic review and analysis. 4. Lead programmatic curriculum development, implementation, and assessment efforts of the graduate program. 5. Engage in scholarly activities and contribute service to the department, college, university, and profession. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS 1. Master\u2019s degree in Physician Assistant Studies. 2. Minimum of three years of full-time experience in higher education at the time of appointment. 3. Current NCCPA certification as a Physician Assistant or NCCPA Emeritus certification status. 4. Currently licensed as a Physician Assistant in the state of Virginia, or eligible for Virginia licensure with the requirement to obtain by the start date. 5. Demonstrated experience mentoring students in an academic and/or professional setting. 6. Commitment to interprofessional education and evidence-based teaching practices. 7. Evidence of an active scholarly agenda and ongoing professional development. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS 1. Record of experience or expertise in teaching a variety of courses in Physician Assistant Studies. 2. Record of leadership experience in a Physician Assistant academic program; special consideration will be given to candidates with experience in continuous programmatic review and assessment. 3. Strong record of scholarly experience. 4. Evidence of professional service. Additional Posting Information: Applicants must submit: (1) a cover letter addressing teaching, leadership, and scholarship experience, (2) a leadership philosophy statement (submitted under \"Other Document #1\" in the JMU application portal), (3) a teaching philosophy statement, (4) a curriculum vitae, and (5) names and contact information for three professional references. JMU\u2019s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 5101bfc2 Last Name (required) 7770a42c Email (required) 93e2fade Job Alert a378b4d7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job