tificate programs. This part-time role supports both the Lifelong Learning Institute (LLI) and Youth Programs within SPCE. The ideal candidate will assist with a variety of programmatic, logistical, and administrative tasks to ensure the success of events, courses, and activities across both programs. Integrated Pest Management Lead Technician 20002370 Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) James Madison University\u2019s Facilities Management is accepting applications for a Integrated Pest Management Technician. Shift is Monday \u2013 Friday, 6:30 a.m. \u2013 3:00 p.m., with overtime as required to cover special events and inclement weather. There is a slightly alternate schedule during the summer months. This position is eligible for a $2,000 sign-on bonus. $1,000 will be paid out after completing six months in the position and the remaining $1,000 will be paid out after completing 12 months in the position. Apply Now First Name (required) 0a857527 Last Name (required) 70fd2400 Email (required) 96fa0ab3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 15fe82bd Last Name (required) 7183151c Email (required) 961a23a4 Job Alert 1f8d0049 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-english-linguistics-tenure-track-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of English: Linguistics - Tenure Track", "description": "Assistant Professor of English: Linguistics - Tenure Track - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of English: Linguistics - Tenure Track - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of English: Linguistics - Tenure Track 20002312 College of Arts and Letters Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Sep 22 2026 Academic Affairs 100020 - English Department Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Assistant Professor of English: Linguistics - Tenure Track State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Arts and Letters Department: 100020 - English Department Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 11/01/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia\u2019s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master\u2019s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Department of English at James Madison University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professorship in Linguistics to begin August 2027. The Department offers a B.A. and an M.A. English and serves students in the university\u2019s General Education program. It houses the University\u2019s thriving creative writing minor, and faculty teach across many interdisciplinary minors, including African, African American and Diaspora Studies; American Studies; Digital Studies; Disability Studies; Environmental Humanities; Film Studies; Latin American, Latinx, and Caribbean Studies; Linguistics; Medieval and Renaissance Studies; Queer Studies; Women\u2019s, Gender and Sexuality Studies; and World Literature. The College of Arts and Letters, in which the Department of English is located, enrolls over 3100 undergraduate majors and about 150 graduate students across ten academic units in the humanities, social sciences, and communication studies. Home to several interdisciplinary centers and institutes, the College employs 270 full-time faculty. We embrace the teacher-scholar model, and encourage excellent applicants within our particular disciplines, as well as scholars and teachers eager to work across them. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to teach introductory, advanced, and graduate (M.A.) courses in Linguistics to English majors and minors, Pre-Professional Secondary Education (SEED) majors and minors, Linguistics minors, and contribute to the university\u2019s General Education Program. This hire will also contribute to the English curriculum by offering literature courses for majors and minors and in the General Education program. Qualifications: Required: \u2022PhD in Linguistics or a related field by August 31, 2027 \u2022Evidence of excellence or potential for excellence in teaching in Linguistics and Literature \u2022Evidence of excellence or potential for excellence in publishing in an area of Linguistics \u2022Evidence of excellence or potential for excellence in departmental, university, or professional service in support of the fields of Linguistics and English Additional Considerations: \u2022We welcome applications from candidates with secondary interest and experience in one or more of the interdisciplinary minors in the College of Arts and Letters. \u2022We welcome applications from candidates with secondary interest and ability in teaching Histories of English. \u2022 We seek candidates with a demonstrated commitment to building a supportive, welcoming scholarly environment. Additional Posting Information: Interested candidate will complete the online application and provide: \u2022Curriculum Vitae \u2022Statement of Teaching Philosophy \u2022Cover Letter \u2022Professional Writing Sample \u2022Names and contact information for three references JMU\u2019s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 782c1425 Last Name (required) b8a83c7e Email (required) 4381c3e3 Job Alert 3f4197fd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interes